post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

  FusionFix is installed but not active yet. Copy it into the game folder
  as your own user, not with sudo:

    gtaiv-eflc-fusionfix-install

  That finds the game in your Steam libraries. For any other copy, pass the
  folder with GTAIV.exe.

  Under Proton or Wine the game must load dinput8.dll from that folder. Set
  this as the game's Steam launch options:

    WINEDLLOVERRIDES="dinput8=n,b" %command%

  Upstream also asks for d3dx9_43 in the game's prefix:

    protontricks 12210 d3dx9_43

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MSG'

  Run gtaiv-eflc-fusionfix-install again to update the copy in your game
  folder.

MSG
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'MSG'

  The copy in your game folder stays. To remove it, delete d3d9.dll,
  d3d9.cfg, dinput8.dll, vulkan.dll and plugins/GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix.*
  there, and update/ unless other mods use it.

MSG
}
